<title>USA: Procter, Paragon settle lawsuits.</title>
<headline>Procter, Paragon settle lawsuits.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co said on Thursday it and Paragon Trade Brands Inc settled lawsuits about P&amp;G patents for feminine protection problems.</p>
<p>The terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Paragon had sued to have the patents declared invalid, or not infringed by Paragon products. P&amp;G counter-sued, claiming infringement.</p>
<p>The settlement leaves the patents intact and provides certain patent licenses to Paragon, P&amp;G said.</p>
<p>In a separate statement, Paragon, of Norcross, Ga., said the settlement permits Paragon to move forward with its new line of store-brand feminine care products, while protecting P&amp;G's proprietary rights.</p>
</text>
